  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A student expanded brackets and obtained the following answers. In each question, identify and correct the student’s mistake and write the correct expansion.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$4(a+b)=4a+b$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The $b$ must also be multiplied by $4$. Correct expansion: $4a+4b$.",
          "worked": "The multiplier $4$ applies to both terms inside the bracket.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4(a+b)&=4\\times a+4\\times b\\\\4(a+b)&=4a+4b\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$5(a+1)=5a+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\times1=5$, not $6$. Correct expansion: $5a+5$.",
          "worked": "Multiply $1$ by $5$ rather than adding $5$ to $1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5(a+1)&=5\\times a+5\\times1\\\\5(a+1)&=5a+5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$8(p-7)=8p+56$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$8\\times(-7)=-56$. Correct expansion: $8p-56$.",
          "worked": "A positive number multiplied by a negative number gives a negative product.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8(p-7)&=8\\times p+8\\times(-7)\\\\8(p-7)&=8p-56\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-3(p-5)=-3p-15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-3)\\times(-5)=15$. Correct expansion: $-3p+15$.",
          "worked": "The product of the two negative numbers is positive.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-3(p-5)&=(-3)\\times p+(-3)\\times(-5)\\\\-3(p-5)&=-3p+15\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$a(a+b)=2a+ab$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a\\times a=a^2$, not $2a$. Correct expansion: $a^2+ab$.",
          "worked": "Multiplying $a$ by itself gives $a^2$; adding $a$ to itself gives $2a$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a(a+b)&=a\\times a+a\\times b\\\\a(a+b)&=a^2+ab\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2m(3m+5)=6m+10m$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2m\\times3m=6m^2$. Correct expansion: $6m^2+10m$.",
          "worked": "The first product contains $m\\times m=m^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2m(3m+5)&=2m\\times3m+2m\\times5\\\\2m(3m+5)&=6m^2+10m\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$-6(x-5)=6x+30$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-6)\\times x=-6x$. Correct expansion: $-6x+30$.",
          "worked": "The negative multiplier makes the first product $-6x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-6(x-5)&=(-6)\\times x+(-6)\\times(-5)\\\\-6(x-5)&=-6x+30\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$3a(4a-7)=12a^2-7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The $-7$ must also be multiplied by $3a$. Correct expansion: $12a^2-21a$.",
          "worked": "Apply the multiplier $3a$ to both terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3a(4a-7)&=3a\\times4a+3a\\times(-7)\\\\3a(4a-7)&=12a^2-21a\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$4a(3a+5)=7a^2+20a$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Multiply the coefficients: $4\\times3=12$, not $7$. Correct expansion: $12a^2+20a$.",
          "worked": "The coefficients in $4a\\times3a$ are multiplied, not added.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4a(3a+5)&=4a\\times3a+4a\\times5\\\\4a(3a+5)&=12a^2+20a\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$3x(2x-7y)=6x^2-21y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3x\\times(-7y)=-21xy$. Correct expansion: $6x^2-21xy$.",
          "worked": "The second product must retain the factor $x$ from $3x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x(2x-7y)&=3x\\times2x+3x\\times(-7y)\\\\3x(2x-7y)&=6x^2-21xy\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
